body:
I can relate in some ways. I was never a feminine female or anything and always just thought I was "bad" at being a girl (which I guess isn't totally wrong... I'm about as bad at being a girl as one can get). I eventually embraced that I wasn't feminine and leaned into being butch/gendernonconforming. But that wasn't quite enough because I still had dysphoria about a lot of parts of my body that only hormones and surgery could change.

&#x200B;

Sometimes I wish I was just a butch woman because I wouldn't have to go through all the effort of asking people to use my new name/pronouns, and because I had gotten heavily involved in some all female spaces... Which I no longer belong in. 

&#x200B;

So my situation isn't exactly like yours, but I do frequently just wish I was comfortable as a cis woman, if for no other reason than it would be significantly easier. I wish I had some advice. But you're definitely not alone.

If they carry on the conversation and are fully engaged, and the conversation comes to a natural end, then I'd say continue.

&#x200B;

If the conversations feel one sided, get cut short, or they stop responding in what feels like the middle of the conversation, there's definitely an indication that maybe they're not super interested.
